OVERVIEW: Promote current captures to baselines.

USAGE: grantiva diff approve [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--platform <platform>] [<screen-names> ...]

ARGUMENTS:
  <screen-names>          Screen names to approve (default: all)

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --platform <platform>   Target platform: ios or android. Defaults to
                          whichever of grantiva.yml / grantiva-android.yml
                          exists, else the project files in this directory.
                          GRANTIVA_PLATFORM also sets it. (values: ios, android)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Create or reuse a named simulator and boot it. `--name` alone reuses
an existing simulator with that name. To create one, the name must contain a
device model ("iPhone 17") or --device-type must be given; the newest installed
runtime is used unless --runtime is passed.

USAGE: grantiva simulator ensure [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] --name <name> [--device-type <device-type>] [--runtime <runtime>] [--boot] [--no-boot]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --name <name>           Simulator name. An existing simulator with this name
                          is reused as-is. When creating, the device type is
                          read from the name if --device-type is omitted, so
                          `--name "iPhone 17"` works on its own.
  --device-type <device-type>
                          Device type name ("iPhone 17 Pro") or identifier.
                          Defaults to the device model named in --name. Checked
                          against an existing simulator only when given.
  --runtime <runtime>     Runtime name, version, identifier, or `latest`.
                          Defaults to the newest installed iOS runtime when
                          creating. Checked against an existing simulator only
                          when given.
  --boot/--no-boot        Boot the simulator and wait for it to be ready. On by
                          default; --no-boot creates it without booting.
                          (default: --boot)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Explicitly delete a named simulator.

USAGE: grantiva simulator delete [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] --name <name>

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --name <name>           Name of the simulator to delete.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: List Grantiva-managed simulator capacity slots.

USAGE: grantiva simulator sessions [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: End a managed session, or reclaim one simulator by UDID when no
ledger entry exists.

A runner session on a torn-down simulator (`grantiva runner start` or `grantiva
run --keep-alive`) is stopped first and its session files are removed; --json
reports it as runnerSessionStopped. The WebDriverAgent xcodebuild and simctl
diagnose the stopped run left writing into the simulator's runner home are then
ended (reapedProcesses in --json) before that home is removed. Without --force,
a process still holding a simulator the teardown deletes or shuts down that it
did not start (a runner, WebDriverAgent's xcodebuild, a simctl diagnose, a
grantiva run) is not killed: a warning on stderr names its pid and command,
--json lists it in leftoverProcesses, and the teardown goes on. --force
reclaims such processes.

USAGE: grantiva simulator teardown [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--session-id <session-id>] [--udid <udid>] [--force]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --session-id <session-id>
                          Ticket/session identifier to shut down and release.
  --udid <udid>           Simulator UDID to reclaim. Use with --force when a
                          run was killed and left processes owning the device.
  --force                 Reclaim by live process inspection instead of the
                          session ledger: kills the grantiva-runner,
                          WebDriverAgent xcodebuild, and simctl diagnose
                          processes holding the simulator, breaks the lease,
                          and reconciles the session registry. Without it, such
                          processes are only named (a stderr warning and
                          leftoverProcesses in --json).
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Delete Grantiva-created simulators that are shut down and not part of
an active session.

USAGE: grantiva simulator cleanup [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Create the AVD when missing (installing its system image first) and
boot it. stdout is the serial, or with --no-boot the AVD name (the serial when
it is already running).

USAGE: grantiva emulator ensure [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--name <name>] [--system-image <system-image>] [--boot] [--no-boot] [--headless]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --name <name>           AVD name. Defaults to emulator in
                          grantiva-android.yml.
  --system-image <system-image>
                          System image package for a new AVD, e.g.
                          "system-images;android-35;google_apis;arm64-v8a".
                          Defaults to system_image in grantiva-android.yml,
                          then that value.
  --boot/--no-boot        Boot the emulator and wait for it to be ready. On by
                          default; --no-boot creates it without booting.
                          (default: --boot)
  --headless              Boot without a window. GRANTIVA_EMULATOR_HEADLESS=1
                          or CI=true does the same; otherwise the emulator gets
                          a window, even when stdout is not a terminal.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Delete an AVD Grantiva created. Others need --force. A running AVD is
never deleted.

USAGE: grantiva emulator delete [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] --name <name> [--force]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --name <name>           AVD name to delete.
  --force                 Delete an AVD Grantiva did not create.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: List the emulators Grantiva started.

USAGE: grantiva emulator sessions [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Kill emulators Grantiva started: one by serial, or all of them. Stops
the UIAutomator2 server and removes the serial's adb forwards first.

A runner session on a torn-down serial (`grantiva runner start` or `grantiva
run --keep-alive`) is stopped too, and its session files are removed; --json
reports it as runnerSessionStopped. The guest's writes are flushed (`adb shell
sync`) before the emulator is killed, so an app installed just before survives
the next boot. Session files of a runner that had already died, and the temp
directories of a killed run on the serial, are removed and listed
(sessionFilesRemoved, temporaryDirectoriesRemoved).

USAGE: grantiva emulator teardown [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--serial <serial>] [--all] [--force]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --serial <serial>       Emulator serial to kill, e.g. emulator-5554.
  --all                   Kill every emulator Grantiva started.
  --force                 Kill the serial even though Grantiva did not start it.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Manage your Grantiva dashboard from the terminal.

USAGE: grantiva console <subcommand>

OPTIONS:
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

SUBCOMMANDS:
  flags, featureflags     Manage feature flags.
  envs                    Manage flag environments (production, staging, ...).
  analytics               Attestation analytics: overview, event log, risk and
                          compliance reports, CSV export.
  devices                 Attested devices: list, filter, and inspect by key ID.
  apps                    Register and manage the apps (bundle IDs) attesting
                          under this organization.
  claims                  Manage the custom claims minted into device JWTs.
  vrt                     Review visual regression runs: approve, reject, and
                          accept or flag individual screens.
  releases                Author the What's New release notes shown to users
                          after they upgrade.
  feedback                Triage feature requests: list, read the thread, set
                          status, reply as the team.
  support                 Work support tickets: list, read the conversation,
                          reply, set status and priority.
  webhooks                Manage webhook endpoints and inspect their deliveries.
  alerts                  Risk alert rules, the attestation failure-rate alert,
                          and notification preferences.
  keys                    Manage API keys. A key can only create keys with
                          scopes it holds itself.
  team                    Members and invites.
  audit                   The organization audit log.
  org                     Organization settings, usage, and billing.
  open                    Open the dashboard in your browser, optionally at an
                          area.

  See 'grantiva help console <subcommand>' for detailed help.
OVERVIEW: Authenticate with Grantiva API.

USAGE: grantiva auth login [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--api-key <api-key>] [--base-url <base-url>]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --api-key <api-key>     API key for Grantiva (skip browser flow)
  --base-url <base-url>   Base URL for Grantiva API (default:
                          https://api.grantiva.io)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Show current authentication status.

USAGE: grantiva auth status [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Remove saved authentication credentials.

USAGE: grantiva auth logout [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
